{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrxbHqShZjEVeQ15cvoV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A package pinned with `==` in the constraints file now keeps its pinned version when that version falls outside the `--max-release-age` window. `tests/test_cooldown.py` passes (38 tests), including a new regression test that fails without the fix.\n\n**Change** (`src/fromager/resolver.py`, `find_all_matching_from_provider`): if the provider's constraint for the requirement is an exact `==` pin, the age cutoff is cleared before filtering. It logs an info line instead of the \"keeping all to avoid empty resolution\" warning. The check sits in one place, so single-version, multi-version, and source resolution all get it.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/test_cooldown.py`):\n- `test_max_release_age_equality_constraint_bypasses_filter` pins `test-pkg==1.2.2` (84 days old, 30-day window) with fallback disabled as in multi-version mode. Before the fix it returned nothing; now it returns `1.2.2`, and the misleading warning is absent.\n- `test_max_release_age_range_constraint_still_filters` checks that a non-`==` constraint (`>=1.0`) still gets the age filter.\n\n**Decisions to confirm:**\n- **Scope is `==` only**, matching the existing cooldown bypass in `resolve_package_cooldown`. A range constraint like `>=1.0` still gets the age heuristic. Widening it to any constraint would be a one-line change, but it would silently disable age filtering for every package with a range constraint.\n- **Only constraints count.** A `==` on a top-level requirement (not in the constraints file) does not bypass the filter, since the ticket is about constraints.\n- **I also updated the how-to doc** (`docs/how-tos/multiple-version-bootstrap.rst`) with one sentence about the exemption. I did not add a `versionchanged` directive because I didn't check the last git tag for the next version. Nothing was committed.\n\n**Checks:** `ruff format --check` and `ruff check` pass on both changed Python files. I could not run `mypy`: the global install is broken and `.venv` doesn't have it. I did not run the full suite."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":128864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f506e136-b8ff-4ee7-a459-e9e96f52a5cc","uuid":"365a511d-3dde-4d73-9462-fdbbb4c25a11","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:13:36.815Z","request_id":"req_011CfrxbHaJxjCjudxthm3fR"}
